Vanessa Bryant is seeking monetary  damages in her wrongful death lawsuit  following the tragic loss of her husband  Kobe Bryant and their daughter Gianna  according to a new case summary filed by  Vanessa on Monday she is asking for  substantial compensation from Island  Express helicopters and claims the  family lost hundreds of millions of  dollars in future earnings from Kobe's  death  now the 38 year old mom of three is  seeking compensation from the company  which owned and operated the helicopter  that crashed claiming the lives of her  husband their 13 year old daughter and  seven others On January 26 and from the  estate of the pilot Aras Obion who also  died in the accident - echo X ray you're  still too low leveled well for off by  following at this time Vanessa  first filed the wrongful death lawsuit  back in March in the original 72 page  lawsuit obtained by ET Kobe's Widow  cited several areas where the pilot may  have been negligent the lawsuit also  alleges that Island Express helicopters  had advanced knowledge of the unfitness  of the pilot due to a previous violation  in 2015 the new case summary which was  filed by Vanessa on Monday indicates  that the lawsuit is currently stalled  pending the release of the National  Transportation Safety Board accident  report which has yet to be generated as  the crash is still under investigation  attorneys for the bayan's estates have  requested a transfer to a county outside  of Los Angeles citing an impartial jury  cannot be impaneled in Los Angeles  Superior Court back in March a company  spokesperson for Island express  helicopters responded to Vanessa's  lawsuit telling ET quote this was a  tragic accident we will have no comment  on the pending litigation as for Vanessa  she's remained strong by spending time  with her daughters and close friends  when ET caught up with her pal Walla  Anthony in April she applauded her for  her strength I tell her every day she's  the strongest woman I know  and I'm really really proud of just how  she's handling everything and just want  to continue to be there you know as much  as I can for her as a friend she's just  an amazing and amazing human being just  just amazing
 

